to remain silent.

250
00:13:31,667 --> 00:13:33,333
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

251
00:13:33,333 --> 00:13:36,933
[FOOTSTEPS APROACHING]

252
00:13:36,933 --> 00:13:37,933
Team!

253
00:13:42,333 --> 00:13:46,567
Ma'am, he's the key to getting
Victor Zafra convicted.

254
00:13:47,333 --> 00:13:48,933
And because you caught
Mr. Chan,

255
00:13:49,500 --> 00:13:50,933
your reputation will finally
be restored.

256
00:13:55,033 --> 00:14:02,000
[DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING]

257
00:14:06,267 --> 00:14:07,200
Lucas?!

258
00:14:07,200 --> 00:14:08,567
- Sir, it's Lucas!
- [DOOR OPENS]

259
00:14:08,567 --> 00:14:09,700
He got shot!

260
00:14:09,700 --> 00:14:11,233
God, what happened?!

261
00:14:11,633 --> 00:14:14,167
- Go and bring him upstairs.
- Arturo,

262
00:14:14,167 --> 00:14:15,967
- call the doctor!
- I already did, Ma'am.

263
00:14:15,967 --> 00:14:17,000
They're on the way here.

264
00:14:18,233 --> 00:14:19,333
[DOOR CLOSES]

265
00:14:20,567 --> 00:14:21,933
[LUCAS GROANING IN PAIN]

266
00:14:21,933 --> 00:14:24,033
- Ow!
- Lucas!

267
00:14:24,033 --> 00:14:25,533
- Careful.
- Lucas!

268
00:14:26,967 --> 00:14:28,833
- Lucas, god!
- Ow...

269
00:14:28,867 --> 00:14:31,167
Here, let me help you.

270
00:14:31,167 --> 00:14:33,900
- Hold on!
- Ow, Ma! It hurts!

271
00:14:33,900 --> 00:14:35,800
- Sorry!
- [GROANING CONTINUES]

272
00:14:35,800 --> 00:14:37,567
Wait. Let's see how bad it is.

273
00:14:37,567 --> 00:14:40,533
Lucas, were you able
to get rid of Mr. Chan?

274
00:14:41,233 --> 00:14:43,333
[DEBORAH] Who shot you?

275
00:14:44,733 --> 00:14:46,633
Ma'am, Sir, Doc Alain is here.

276
00:14:47,233 --> 00:14:48,567
- [GROANING CONTINUES]
- Excuse me.

277
00:14:48,567 --> 00:14:49,933
- [DEBORAH] He's here.
- Excuse me, please.

278
00:14:49,933 --> 00:14:50,900
Doc.

279
00:14:53,133 --> 00:14:55,167
- Please excuse me.
- Be careful!

280
00:14:55,167 --> 00:14:56,233
- I'm sorry for this.
- Do be careful.

281
00:14:56,233 --> 00:15:00,667
[GROANING CONTINUES]

282
00:15:00,667 --> 00:15:01,700
[DEBORAH] Is he okay?

283
00:15:02,967 --> 00:15:04,567
I'll take it from here.

284
00:15:04,567 --> 00:15:06,200
Please give us some space.

285
00:15:07,000 --> 00:15:09,000
Alright. Lay down for a bit.

286
00:15:10,333 --> 00:15:13,400
[GROANING IN PAIN]

287
00:15:13,400 --> 00:15:15,100
- [SQUELCHES]
- [DOOR OPENS]

288
00:15:15,100 --> 00:15:17,100
[GRIM MUSIC PLAYING]

289
00:15:17,100 --> 00:15:18,100
[DOOR CLOSES]

290
00:15:18,333 --> 00:15:20,500
- Ma'am, I'm sorry--
- Imbecile!

291
00:15:22,233 --> 00:15:25,033
Didn't I entrust Lucas to you?
Huh?!

292
00:15:25,033 --> 00:15:26,133
Ma'am, Lucas was already shot--

293
00:15:26,133 --> 00:15:28,533
Because you were too slow!

294
00:15:28,533 --> 00:15:30,733
If only you were quicker,

295
00:15:30,733 --> 00:15:32,433
you would have saved him!

296
00:15:32,433 --> 00:15:34,467
You could have saved him!

297
00:15:36,367 --> 00:15:37,767
- Ma'am!
- Useless!

298
00:15:37,767 --> 00:15:38,933
- [MARIANO] That's enough!
- [BLOW LANDS]

299
00:15:38,933 --> 00:15:40,467
- [THUDS]
- [MARIANO] Enough.

300
00:15:40,467 --> 00:15:42,567
It should have been you!

301
00:15:42,567 --> 00:15:43,833
I said, enough!

302
00:15:43,833 --> 00:15:46,467
- [GUNSHOTS]
- [DEBORAH GRUNTS]

303
00:15:46,467 --> 00:15:48,633
- Let go of me!
- Give me that!

304
00:15:48,933 --> 00:15:50,133
Calm down!

305
00:15:50,133 --> 00:15:57,100
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

306
00:16:01,967 --> 00:16:04,033
- [MR. CHAN]<i> No! Don't touch me!
</i>- [CASTOR] Shut up!

307
00:16:04,033 --> 00:16:06,467
[MR. CHAN] Call my lawyer!
I'll call my lawyer!

308
00:16:06,467 --> 00:16:07,900
- Let me go!
- What now, ma'am?

309
00:16:07,900 --> 00:16:09,800
We won't be able to keep
this from Sir Delgado.

310
00:16:09,833 --> 00:16:11,800
I think he'll be pleased
with this anyway.

311
00:16:12,700 --> 00:16:13,833
- Sam!
- What the?

312
00:16:13,833 --> 00:16:15,600
So you guys did go to Mr. Chan.

313
00:16:16,167 --> 00:16:18,000
[SEBASTIAN] Huh?
Are you guys alright?

314
00:16:18,000 --> 00:16:20,400
Bring Karen to the clinic.
Get yourselves checked too.

315
00:16:20,400 --> 00:16:21,667
- Go on.
- Mm-hmm.

316
00:16:21,933 --> 00:16:23,933
Karen, what happened?
Were you shot?

317
00:16:23,933 --> 00:16:26,400
[SARCASTICALLY] You noticed?
You're right on target.

318
00:16:26,400 --> 00:16:28,033
You shot my heart too.

319
00:16:28,033 --> 00:16:29,400
Want me to shoot you for real?

320
00:16:31,200 --> 00:16:32,833
[CLICKS TONGUE] Sam,

321
00:16:32,833 --> 00:16:33,800
[GRUNTS]

322
00:16:34,200 --> 00:16:35,900
you know I could have
helped you.

323
00:16:35,900 --> 00:16:38,933
I wish you told me about it.
Look at what happened to them!

324
00:16:38,933 --> 00:16:41,000
What's important is we captured
Mr. Chan.

325
00:16:41,667 --> 00:16:42,933
- Let's go.
- Jacinto.

326
00:16:43,433 --> 00:16:45,067
What is the meaning of this?

327
00:16:45,067 --> 00:16:48,567
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

328
00:16:48,567 --> 00:16:50,133
Sir, there was just a bit
of trouble.

329
00:16:50,133 --> 00:16:51,667
But we finally got Mr. Chan.

330
00:16:51,667 --> 00:16:53,600
Aren't you supposed to be
hands off from the case?

331
00:16:54,033 --> 00:16:55,767
Don't you understand
what it means?!

332
00:16:55,767 --> 00:16:57,633
I'm just doing my job.

333
00:16:57,633 --> 00:17:01,167
Jacinto, your job
is to honor my commands.

334
00:17:02,467 --> 00:17:05,033
Sebastian, take care
of Mr. Chan.

335
00:17:06,867 --> 00:17:07,900
Sam.

336
00:17:07,900 --> 00:17:09,167
- [SEBASTIAN] Sir.
- [MR. CHAN] Impossible!

337
00:17:09,167 --> 00:17:11,067
In my office, now!

338
00:17:12,000 --> 00:17:13,700
- [SEBASTIAN] This way.
- [MR. CHAN] Let me go!

339
00:17:13,700 --> 00:17:15,400
- Let me go!
- Stop struggling!

340
00:17:15,433 --> 00:17:20,833
- My lawyer! I need my lawyer!
- Come on, follow us.

341
00:17:20,833 --> 00:17:27,767
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

342
00:17:34,100 --> 00:17:35,533
What did really happen?

343
00:17:35,533 --> 00:17:37,833
Boss, when we arrived
at Mr. Chan's warehouse,

344
00:17:37,833 --> 00:17:40,267
we immediately attacked
his group.

345
00:17:40,267 --> 00:17:42,600
But suddenly, a group
of NCIA agents arrived.

346
00:17:42,600 --> 00:17:44,100
We had to engage with them.

347
00:17:44,100 --> 00:17:46,167
We're not sure if the police
we encountered

348
00:17:46,167 --> 00:17:48,367
are Mr. Chan's men.

349
00:17:49,167 --> 00:17:50,933
It's like they knew
we were coming.

350
00:17:50,933 --> 00:17:52,167
[SCOFFS]

351
00:17:52,167 --> 00:17:53,700
Leave.

352
00:17:54,300 --> 00:17:55,733
You...

353
00:17:56,300 --> 00:18:00,733
all reek of incompetence!

354
00:18:00,733 --> 00:18:02,633
Get out of my face!

355
00:18:02,967 --> 00:18:03,900
Get out.

356
00:18:04,367 --> 00:18:06,000
Get out!

357
00:18:07,600 --> 00:18:08,767
Out!

358
00:18:10,233 --> 00:18:11,867
Get out!

359
00:18:11,867 --> 00:18:18,833
[BREATHING HEAVILY]

360
00:18:24,433 --> 00:18:31,400
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

361
00:18:36,633 --> 00:18:37,600
[DOOR SLAMS CLOSE]

362
00:18:38,633 --> 00:18:40,300
You didn't follow my orders.

363
00:18:40,733 --> 00:18:42,500
You didn't follow the protocol!

364
00:18:42,700 --> 00:18:45,600
Sir, I can't stand just
lounging around in the office

365
00:18:45,600 --> 00:18:46,800
doing nothing!

366
00:18:46,800 --> 00:18:49,200
All while those involved
in the gold smuggling case

367
00:18:49,200 --> 00:18:50,333
is roaming around freely!

368
00:18:50,333 --> 00:18:53,267
You're no longer handling
the gold smuggling case!

369
00:18:54,433 --> 00:18:56,133
What did I tell you, huh?

370
00:18:57,467 --> 00:18:59,333
You are hands off on this case!

371
00:19:00,667 --> 00:19:02,400
Why did you disobey me?

372
00:19:04,633 --> 00:19:06,000
What do you want to prove?

373
00:19:06,467 --> 00:19:08,267
That I can solve this case.

374
00:19:09,900 --> 00:19:10,967
No, Sam.

375
00:19:12,500 --> 00:19:15,867
You've proven
how stubborn you are!

376
00:19:16,600 --> 00:19:19,767
You've proven
that you don't listen

377
00:19:19,767 --> 00:19:22,100
to those who are above you!

378
00:19:24,600 --> 00:19:28,533
And you even dragged
your colleagues into this.

379
00:19:32,800 --> 00:19:33,967
You know what, Sam,

380
00:19:35,733 --> 00:19:39,633
I was already working on
not getting you suspended

381
00:19:39,633 --> 00:19:42,467
because of Pia's report.

382
00:19:46,933 --> 00:19:50,067
But because
of what you've done...

383
00:19:50,633 --> 00:19:52,733
But because of what
all of you have done,

384
00:19:52,733 --> 00:19:56,200
you won't just get a suspension,

385
00:19:56,933 --> 00:20:00,400
you and your whole team might
get dismissed from service!

386
00:20:01,200 --> 00:20:02,633
Sir, wait a minute.

387
00:20:03,133 --> 00:20:04,867
Please don't involve
the whole team.

388
00:20:04,867 --> 00:20:07,600
I encouraged them
to work with me on this.

389
00:20:07,600 --> 00:20:09,933
If there's someone to blame,
then let it be me.

390
00:20:13,167 --> 00:20:14,367
[DELGADO SIGHS]

391
00:20:14,367 --> 00:20:21,333
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

392
00:20:31,967 --> 00:20:32,867
Sam.

393
00:20:36,033 --> 00:20:37,100
Do you know that

394
00:20:38,100 --> 00:20:40,700
I see you as my own daughter?

395
00:20:47,133 --> 00:20:48,700
But do you know what, Sam,

396
00:20:49,933 --> 00:20:52,000
just how painful

397
00:20:56,533 --> 00:20:58,033
was your disobedience?

398
00:20:58,033 --> 00:21:05,000
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

399
00:21:05,000 --> 00:21:06,233
Oh, sir?

400
00:21:10,067 --> 00:21:13,433
I know what we did was wrong
but we did it anyways.

401
00:21:15,367 --> 00:21:16,467
I'm sorry.

402
00:21:20,700 --> 00:21:23,200
I knew I have my own mistakes
and shortcomings.

403
00:21:24,567 --> 00:21:27,967
But whatever you decide
on, I'll accept it.

404
00:21:29,500 --> 00:21:30,667
But please just punish me.

405
00:21:31,100 --> 00:21:32,500
Not the whole team.

406
00:21:32,500 --> 00:21:39,467
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

407
00:21:43,567 --> 00:21:48,467
[MOTORCYCLE ENGINE REVVING]

408
00:21:48,600 --> 00:21:49,567
[ENGINE STOPS]

409
00:21:54,967 --> 00:22:01,967
[INTRIGUING MUSIC PLAYING]

410
00:22:24,033 --> 00:22:25,400
- He brought it home?
- Mm-hmm.

411
00:22:27,933 --> 00:22:29,000
I knew it.

412
00:22:29,133 --> 00:22:30,267
[KEYS JANGLING]

413
00:22:30,400 --> 00:22:31,300
[DOOR OPENS]

414
00:22:38,900 --> 00:22:40,267
[DOOR CREAKS, CLOSES]

415
00:22:49,167 --> 00:22:52,300
[SCOFFS]
Gabo can't really be trusted.

416
00:22:53,167 --> 00:22:54,033
[LINE RINGING]

417
00:22:54,167 --> 00:22:57,700
[PHONE RINGING]

418
00:22:58,767 --> 00:23:00,233
- Hello?
- [UWAK] Omeng.

419
00:23:00,933 --> 00:23:01,933
Gabo is here.

420
00:23:02,000 --> 00:23:02,967
He has the gold.

421
00:23:03,100 --> 00:23:04,333
He brought it inside his house.

422
00:23:08,500 --> 00:23:09,433
Why?

423
00:23:09,567 --> 00:23:10,967
Lawin just called.

424
00:23:11,100 --> 00:23:12,067
It's about Gabo...

425
00:23:12,700 --> 00:23:13,833
he ran away with the gold.

426
00:23:13,967 --> 00:23:19,333
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

427
00:23:19,467 --> 00:23:20,667
[LUGGAGE CLICKS]

428
00:23:39,900 --> 00:23:41,700
[SNICKERS]

429
00:23:41,833 --> 00:23:44,700
Gabo wouldn't do that.
I know him well.

430
00:23:45,300 --> 00:23:46,567
It's too soon to tell.

431
00:23:47,800 --> 00:23:49,867
Let's not judge him yet.

432
00:23:54,100 --> 00:24:01,100
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

433
00:24:06,133 --> 00:24:10,067
[MUSIC TURNS SOMBER]

434
00:24:20,033 --> 00:24:23,233
[BETCHAY] Time is running out
for your father.

435
00:24:23,767 --> 00:24:24,967
<i> Pa!</i>

436
00:24:25,100 --> 00:24:28,333
<i>It's not like your father
expects anything of you either.</i>

437
00:24:29,867 --> 00:24:30,867
<i> Pa!</i>

438
00:24:32,200 --> 00:24:35,233
[BETCHAY]
<i> Money! We need money!</i>

439
00:24:46,100 --> 00:24:51,700
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

440
00:24:51,700 --> 00:24:53,967
Gabo isn't really to be trusted.

441
00:24:53,967 --> 00:24:56,067
<i> He ran away with the gold.</i>

442
00:24:56,200 --> 00:24:57,300
<i> What do we do now?</i>

443
00:24:57,300 --> 00:25:00,067
<i>I'm not going to get back
at Mr. Chan, Ma.</i>

444
00:25:00,200 --> 00:25:02,033
<i> But to the person who shot me!</i>

445
00:25:02,200 --> 00:25:03,667
I'll make Samantha Jacinto pay.

446
00:25:03,800 --> 00:25:06,167
<i>Talking won't work
on Ricardo anymore.</i>

447
00:25:06,300 --> 00:25:07,567
<i>We need to negotiate
the hard way.</i>

448
00:25:07,700 --> 00:25:08,567
<i> Someone was there</i>

449
00:25:08,700 --> 00:25:10,167
<i>that's why we caught
Mr. Chan easily.</i>

450
00:25:10,300 --> 00:25:13,767
Could it be the same mystery man
<i> who helped us catch Tiger?</i>

451
00:25:13,900 --> 00:25:14,767
<i> The question is, who is he?</i>

452
00:25:14,900 --> 00:25:16,167
<i> You know how his mind works.</i>

453
00:25:16,300 --> 00:25:18,467
<i>He's from Ginintuang Lupa
after all.</i>

454
00:25:18,600 --> 00:25:20,100
<i>I have the money
for Papa's surgery.</i>

455
00:25:20,233 --> 00:25:22,033
<i>I won't let anything bad
happen to my father.</i>

456
00:25:22,167 --> 00:25:23,533
<i>I'll do everything
to keep him alive.</i>

457
00:25:23,667 --> 00:25:24,667
<i> Where did you get the money?</i>

458
00:25:24,933 --> 00:25:26,733
What kind of job? Was it legal?

459
00:25:26,933 --> 00:25:28,033
<i> He'll be easily tempted.</i>

460
00:25:28,167 --> 00:25:30,700
<i>With that much gold, for sure,
he was blinded by greed.</i>
